                  <d6p1:EnginePropertyDefinition>
                    <d6p1:fields xmlns:d11p1="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays">
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>Name</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Shapes.Shape3D.DepthRenderingMode</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>EngineDefined</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>True</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>ExportToEngine</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>True</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>OwnerClass</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Kanzi.Shapes.Shape3D</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>EngineDefaultValue</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>2</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>DefaultValue</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>2</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>EngineType</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Int</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>DisplayName</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Depth Rendering Mode</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>Tooltip</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Sets the depth rendering mode used by a 3D shape:
- Normal uses Kanzi default rendering.
- Depth Offset uses the Fill Depth Offset and Stroke Depth Offset properties to apply a depth offset.
- Two Pass Rendering first renders the depth of the shape and in a second pass renders the color of the shape. The second pass uses the Fill Depth Offset and Stroke Depth Offset properties to apply a depth offset. This is the default.
- Depth Write Disabled disables the depth write completely for both fill and stroke.</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>ValueProvider</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Enum:Normal |0;Depth Offset |1;Two Pass Rendering |2;Depth Write Disabled |3</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>Host</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Kanzi.Shapes.Shape3D:context,Kanzi.Shapes.SVGImage3D:context,Kanzi.Node3D:user</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                    </d6p1:fields>
                  </d6p1:EnginePropertyDefinition>
                  <d6p1:EnginePropertyDefinition>
                    <d6p1:fields xmlns:d11p1="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays">
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>Name</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Shapes.Shape3D.FillDepthOffset</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>EngineDefined</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>True</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>ExportToEngine</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>True</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>OwnerClass</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Kanzi.Shapes.Shape3D</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>EngineDefaultValue</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>0.000000,0.000000</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>DefaultValue</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>0, -3</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>EngineType</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Vector2</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>DisplayName</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Fill Depth Offset</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>Tooltip</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Sets the polygon depth offset used by the fill of a 3D shape node:
- Derivative Multiplier sets the multiplier of the depth change for the fragment.
- Constant Multiplier multiplies the smallest measurable unit of depth, dependent on the target platform.

You can use the offset to render filled shapes on the surface of other shapes without z-fighting. Kanzi typically shows nearer the camera those polygons that have a negative offset.
</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>Editor</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Vector2dSliderEditor.PolygonDepthOffsetEditor</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>Host</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Kanzi.Shapes.Shape3D:context</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>LowerBound</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>-32, -32</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>UpperBound</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>32, 32</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>Step</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>0.1, 0.1</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                    </d6p1:fields>
                  </d6p1:EnginePropertyDefinition>
                  <d6p1:EnginePropertyDefinition>
                    <d6p1:fields xmlns:d11p1="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays">
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>Name</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>Shapes.Shape3D.StrokeDepthOffset</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                        <d11p1:Key>EngineDefined</d11p1:Key>
                        <d11p1:Value>True</d11p1:Value>
                      </d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
                      <d11p1:KeyValueOfstringstring>
